---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Grab Scanner privacy policy" description="Privacy policy for the Grab Scanner household tool." noindex>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-10 sm:px-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="prose-body">
      <h1>Grab Scanner privacy policy</h1>
      <p><em>Last updated 4 October 2026</em></p>

      <p>
        Grab Scanner is a private, non-commercial tool used by one household to summarise its own Grab
        spending. This policy explains what it does with Google user data.
      </p>

      <h2>What data it accesses</h2>
      <p>
        When a family member signs in with Google, they grant the read-only Gmail permission
        (<code>gmail.readonly</code>). The tool uses it only to search for messages from
        <code>no-reply@grab.com</code> whose subject contains "receipt", and to download those messages.
        It does not read, download or store any other e-mail. It cannot send, change or delete mail.
      </p>

      <h2>How the data is used</h2>
      <p>
        Receipt contents (date, amount, ride route and distance, merchant and items ordered, fees) are
        parsed into a spending report for the household. Nothing is used for advertising, profiling,
        resale or to train AI or machine-learning models.
      </p>

      <h2>Where it is stored and who can see it</h2>
      <p>
        The tool runs only on a personal computer belonging to the household. Downloaded receipts, the
        report and the Google access tokens are stored on that computer's disk and are not uploaded to any
        server. The report is shared only with the family members whose receipts it contains. No data is
        sold or transferred to anyone else.
      </p>

      <h2>Keeping and deleting data</h2>
      <p>
        Receipts are kept for as long as the household uses the tool. A family member can ask for their data
        to be deleted at any time, and it will be removed from the computer. Anyone can also withdraw access
        immediately at <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">myaccount.google.com/permissions</a>.
        Once access is withdrawn, the tool can no longer read their mail.
      </p>

      <h2>Google API Services User Data Policy</h2>
      <p>
        Grab Scanner's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or deletion requests: use the support e-mail address shown on the Google sign-in screen
        for Grab Scanner.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
